OP_REGION_TO_POOL zeroes the whole range, work in its size,
and no longer says so where it calls memset,
so the walk in the table of "Bounded work" hides behind a call.
It zeroes the same memory, so only the loop check catches it.

Caught-by: loop-bounds

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -147,3 +147,2 @@
         /* From here on the memory is the kernel's. */
-        CALL_WALK(memset);
         memset(p2v(base), 0, size);
